Quickly select boundaries for sending a reply as separate messages.
The input is JSON: text is the original reply; candidates are precomputed boundaries. Each id is a candidate number, and before/after show the surrounding original text.
Return only a JSON object such as {{"break_after": [1, 3]}}. Use candidate ids in increasing order without duplicates.
Do not return or rewrite sentences, calculate character offsets, explain, or use Markdown.
Select natural semantic boundaries only. Do not split parentheses, quotations, emoticons, links, code, or formulas.
For short replies, complete code, formulas, or passages better read together, return {{"break_after": []}}.

{payload}
